      "message": "nit: if `groupIds` is big the we might consider iterating over it instead of copying it all to array e.g.\n```\n  @Override\n  public Collection\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e parentGroupsOf(Set\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e groupIds) {\n    try {\n      Set\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e parents \u003d new HashSet\u003c\u003e();\n      for (BatchIterator iterator \u003d new BatchIterator(groupIds, indexConfig.maxTerms());\n          iterator.hasNext(); ) {\n        parentGroups.getAll(iterator.next()).values().forEach(p -\u003e parents.addAll(p));\n      }\n      return parents;\n    } catch (ExecutionException e) {\n      logger.atWarning().withCause(e).log(\"Cannot load included groups\");\n      return Collections.emptySet();\n    }\n  }\n\n  private static class BatchIterator implements Iterator\u003cList\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e\u003e {\n    private final Iterator\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e source;\n    private final int batchSize;\n\n    private BatchIterator(Set\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e groupIds, int batchSize) {\n      this.source \u003d groupIds.iterator();\n      this.batchSize \u003d batchSize;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public boolean hasNext() {\n      return source.hasNext();\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public List\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e next() {\n      List\u003cAccountGroup.UUID\u003e batch \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e(batchSize);\n      int count \u003d 0;\n      while (source.hasNext() \u0026\u0026 count++ \u003c batchSize) {\n        batch.add(source.next());\n      }\n      return batch;\n    }\n  }\n```\nWDYT?",
